rows.09:3698:
Thinking they must have bolted in a hurry, he swept the light all around, but there was no sign of anyone.
Even if they had bolted, he should have caught that moment with his own eyes, and anyone moving at any real speed could not have kept the floorboards from creaking.
And yet he sensed nothing of the kind.{p}

rows.09:3d34:
"Where? Where are you?!"
Shouting that, Mr. Sakurai ran all over the old school building.
And no matter how fast he ran, the footsteps followed him precisely, always keeping the same distance.{p}

rows.09:4fb8:
When she reached the third floor and shone her flashlight ahead, the corridor stretched on far longer than she'd expected.
One by one, she shone the flashlight into each classroom.
"Huh. Looks like there's nothing to it after all."{p}

rows.09:5430:
She managed to get through the second floor safely too, and it was while she was going down the stairs to the first floor.
She could feel air unlike anything before sweeping right through her.
She could clearly feel her pores tightening and every hair on her body standing on end.{p}"Ugh. What is this feeling...?"{p}

rows.09:5604:
Something hazy seemed to be coming toward her from the far end of the corridor.
"...?"
When she turned to look once more, this time she could see what it was.{p}

rows.09:56d8:
A baby on all fours, grinning from ear to ear, was heading straight for her.
Incredibly fast...
"Wh-what is that thing?!"{p}

rows.09:57ac:
She couldn't help quickening her pace.
For some reason, though, she couldn't run.
She felt that if she ran, things would suddenly come to a head, so she couldn't bring herself to upset this balance.{p}
